> lysis. (Tip: use keepusing() to specify which variables to keep from the usin
> g dataset; the default is all.)
.         keep cid pid hid syear parid partner sex gebjahr 

.         
.         * biobirth contains information on fertility history
.         merge m:1 pid using "$IN/biobirth.dta", nogen keep(master matches) 
(variable pid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable cid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable gebjahr was int, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label sex already defined)
(label sex_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

.         
.         * pl contains all variables from the individual questionnaire
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pl.dta", nogen keepusing(plh030* pmoni
> n) keep(master matches)
(label cid already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. 
.         label language EN // change language of the labels to English

. 
.         save "$DATA/h1_dataset.dta", replace // save merged dataset
file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/5%-sample/h1_dataset.dta saved

. 
. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
.         *First we needed to determine which attitude variables would be part 
> of the attitude-scale (based on cronbachs alpha); this we checked on the full
>  sample before following any excludion criteria. See the procedure below that
>  is commented out (line 67-110). After checking which variables should be inc
> luded, we followed the same procedure starting on line 172 - but this time us
> ing the final analytical sample.
.         
.          use "$DATA/h1_dataset.dta", clear //use full sample to calculate cro
> nbachs alpha

. 
.         /*
>         keep if syear ==2012 //items asked in 2012 survey
> 
>         //replace missings with "." (negative values refer to missings)
>         //reverse code some variables (plh0303 plh0304 plh0308_v1 plh0309) to
>  make higher score more gender equal
>                  
>                 *Women Should Rather Care About Family Than Career (1 Stimme 
> voll zu /4 Stimme ueberhaupt nicht zu) 
>                 replace plh0301 = . if plh0301<0 
> 
>                 *Kind unter 3 J. leidet wenn Mutter arbeitet (FID) [2012] (1 
> Stimme voll zu /4 Stimme ueberhaupt nicht zu)
>                 replace plh0302_v1 = . if plh0302_v1 <0
> 
>                 *Men Involved in Housework (1 Stimme voll zu /4 Stimme ueberh
> aupt nicht zu)
>                 replace plh0303 = . if plh0303 <0
>                         revrs plh0303 
>                         drop plh0303
>                          
>                 *Children Suffer When Father Focused On Career //(1 Stimme vo
> ll zu /4 Stimme ueberhaupt nicht zu)
>                 replace plh0304 = . if plh0304 <0 
>                         revrs plh0304 
>                         drop plh0304 
> 
>                 *Men Care more About Financial Security (1 Stimme voll zu /4 
> Stimme ueberhaupt nicht zu)
>                 replace plh0307 = . if plh0307 <0 
> 
>                 *Mann/Frau in gleich in Arbeit u. Haushalt/Familie (FID) [201
> 2] (1 Stimme voll zu /4 Stimme ueberhaupt nicht zu) 
>                 replace plh0308_v1 = . if plh0308_v1 <0
>                         revrs plh0308_v1 
>                         drop plh0308_v1
> 
>                 *Working Mothers Equal Emotional (1 Stimme voll zu /4 Stimme 
> ueberhaupt nicht zu)
>                 replace plh0309 = . if plh0309 <0
>                         revrs plh0309 
>                         drop plh0309
>                                 
>         * Check Cronbachs alpha >= 0.7
>         factor plh0301 plh0302_v1 revplh0303 revplh0304 plh0307 revplh0308_v1
>  revplh0309  //Factor1 eigenvalue 1.9, suggested factor 1.
>         alpha  plh0301 plh0302_v1 revplh0303 revplh0304 plh0307 revplh0308_v1
>  revplh0309, item 
> 
>         *Item 304 does not fit (also loads onto factor3 on its own, and is ve
> ry unique)
>         *Alpha currently 0.67
>         *If remove item plh0304 (Children Suffer When Father Focused On Caree
> r), new alpha 0.72
>         alpha plh0301 plh0302_v1 revplh0303 plh0307 revplh0308_v1 revplh0309,
>  item //new alpha: 0.72
>         */
. 
. 
. * FILTERS * 
. 
.         *Only keep participants who:
.         *(1) have children
.         *(2) have one child only (drop observations once second child arrives
> ). Twins counted as 'having daughter' if at least both are girls.
.         *(3) use last year of panel where we have full information 
. 
.         use "$DATA/h1_dataset.dta", clear 

.         
.                 *(1a) Keep only participants who have children:
.                 fre kidgeb01

kidgeb01 -- Year Of Birth 1st. Child
