              |      Freq.    Percent      Valid       Cum.
--------------+--------------------------------------------
Valid   0     |         29      48.33      48.33      48.33
        1     |         31      51.67      51.67     100.00
        Total |         60     100.00     100.00           
-----------------------------------------------------------

.         label variable d_sex "Sex of participants (0=Male, 1=Female)"

. 
.         *Generate dummy variable for whether participant`s child is a girl (1
> ) or boy (0)
.         gen d_daughter = 1 if kidsex01== 2 //girl
(32 missing values generated)

.         replace d_daughter=0 if kidsex01==1 //boy       
(32 real changes made)

.         drop if twins==1 & d_daughter==0 & kidsex02==2 //drop if first child 
> is boy, but second twin is girl 
(0 observations deleted)

.         drop if twins==1 & d_daughter==1 & kidsex02==1 //drop if first child 
> is girl, but second twin is boy 
(0 observations deleted)

.         label variable d_daughter "Sex of first child (0=son, 1=daughter)"

.         fre d_daughter

d_daughter -- Sex of first child (0=son, 1=daughter)
-----------------------------------------------------------
              |      Freq.    Percent      Valid       Cum.
--------------+--------------------------------------------
Valid   0     |         32      53.33      53.33      53.33
        1     |         28      46.67      46.67     100.00
        Total |         60     100.00     100.00           
-----------------------------------------------------------

.         
.         *Select gender attitude items for scale construction 
.         
.         *Based on previous test of cronbachs alpha on the whole sample, keep 
> only relevant 'gender attitude items'
.         *replace missings with "." (negative values refer to missings)
.         *reverse code some variables (plh0303 plh0304 plh0308_v1 plh0309) to 
> make higher score refer to more gender equal
.          
.                 *Women Should Rather Care About Family Than Career (1 Stimme 
> voll zu /4 Stimme ueberhaupt nicht zu) 
.                 replace plh0301 = . if plh0301<0 
(29 real changes made, 29 to missing)

.                 
.                 *Kind unter 3 J. leidet wenn Mutter arbeitet (FID) [2012] (1 
> Stimme voll zu /4 Stimme ueberhaupt nicht zu)
.                 replace plh0302_v1 = . if plh0302_v1 <0
(29 real changes made, 29 to missing)

. 
.                 *Men Involved in Housework (1 Stimme voll zu /4 Stimme ueberh
> aupt nicht zu)
.                 replace plh0303 = . if plh0303 <0
(29 real changes made, 29 to missing)

.                 revrs plh0303 

.                 drop plh0303

.                                          
.                 *Men Care more About Financial Security (1 Stimme voll zu /4 
> Stimme ueberhaupt nicht zu)
.                 replace plh0307 = . if plh0307 <0 
(29 real changes made, 29 to missing)

. 
.                 *Mann/Frau in gleich in Arbeit u. Haushalt/Familie (FID) [201
> 2] (1 Stimme voll zu /4 Stimme ueberhaupt nicht zu) 
.                 replace plh0308_v1 = . if plh0308_v1 <0
(29 real changes made, 29 to missing)

.                 revrs plh0308_v1 

.                 drop plh0308_v1

. 
.                 *Working Mothers Equal Emotional (1 Stimme voll zu /4 Stimme 
> ueberhaupt nicht zu)
.                 replace plh0309 = . if plh0309 <0
(30 real changes made, 30 to missing)

.                 revrs plh0309 

.                 drop plh0309

. 
.                 
.         *Construct the gender attitude scale that will be our dependent varia
> ble:
. 
.                 *Take the mean of all items. At least 4 items need to be answ
> ered
.                 egen numnomissing = rownonmiss(plh0301 plh0302_v1 revplh0303 
> plh0307 revplh0308_v1 revplh0309) //how many items present (not missing)

.                 egen attitude_scale = rowmean(plh0301 plh0302_v1 revplh0303 p
> lh0307 revplh0308_v1 revplh0309) if numnomissing >=4
(36 missing values generated)

.                 sum attitude_scale 

    Variable |        Obs        Mean    Std. dev.       Min        Max
-------------+---------------------------------------------------------
attitude_s~e |         24    2.301389    .6787655   1.166667        3.5

. 
.                 *Convert to scale: 0-1
.                 gen attitude_scale_01 = (attitude_scale - r(min)) / (r(max) -
>  r(min))
(36 missing values generated)

. 
. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * 
. 
.         * We assume that a scale composing of various items in support for ge
> nder equality (attitude_scale_01) is a good measure of support for gender equ
> ality (hypothesis 1), 
.         * if having a daughter, the respondent more strongly supports gender 
> equality (has a higher score on the 0-1 scale).
.         * Accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with `attitude
> _scale_01' as the dependent variable and the dummy variable `d_daughter' as t
> he independent variable
. 
. 
. reg attitude_scale_01 d_daughter, cluster(hid)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =         24
                                                F(1, 15)          =       0.10
                                                Prob > F          =     0.7561
                                                R-squared         =     0.0074
                                                Root MSE          =     .29633

                                   (Std. err. adjusted for 16 clusters in hid)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
             |               Robust
attitude_~01 | Coefficient  std. err.      t    P>|t|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
  d_daughter |   .0492507    .155655     0.32   0.756      -.28252    .3810215
       _cons |   .4637363     .09685     4.79   0.000     .2573054    .6701671
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * 
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[d_daughter] / _se[d_daughter]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation based of directionality and p-value
.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

. 
. 
